FIX Performance Session Layer
-----------------------------

src/fixp/schema/*.yaml, src/fixp/datamodel/, project/ and docs/schema/
model the FIX Performance Session Layer (FIXP), Version 1.0 Technical
Standard, by FIX Protocol Limited (FIX Trading Community):
https://github.com/FIXTradingCommunity/fixp-specification. They are this
project's work, written in its own words. They are not FIX Protocol
Limited's, and their use does not imply endorsement by FIX Protocol
Limited. "FIX", "FIX Protocol" and "FIX Trading Community" are marks of FIX
Protocol Limited, used here to identify the standard.

FIX Protocol Limited licenses the FIXP specification and its resource files
under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivatives 4.0 International
Public License (CC BY-ND 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nd/4.0/legalcode). That licence
lets anyone copy and share the work unchanged, with credit and a link to
the licence. It does not let anyone share an adapted version.

upstream/fixp-specification/ therefore holds these files whole and
unchanged, each matched by git object hash in scripts/upstream_pins.tsv:

  (c) Copyright 2014-2021 FIX Protocol Ltd., under CC BY-ND 4.0:
    v1-0-STANDARD/resources/FixRepositoryForFIXP.xml
    v1-0-STANDARD/resources/OrchestraForFIXP.xml
    v1-0-STANDARD/resources/SBEschemaForFIXP.xml
    at the tag v1.0-STANDARD, commit 6d89f5f.

  LICENSE, the text of CC BY-ND 4.0 as that repository publishes it.

These copies are outside this repository's Apache License, and this project
claims no right over them.

Nothing else here repeats or adapts FIX's text. What the schema takes from
FIX is the message, field and value names, their numbers, and the
structure, which a FIXP implementation must use to work with FIXP at all.
Copyright protects the way FIX expressed its specification, not the
methods, procedures and facts it describes, and CC BY-ND 4.0 restricts
nothing that copyright does not (its section 8(a)).

The project nevertheless takes the stricter reading that European law
allows (Infopaq, C-5/08), under which even a short extract can be protected
when it shows its author's own choices. Every title, description and comment
was written from what the element does, in the project's own words, not by
rewording FIX's sentences. tests/test_own_words.py finds any run of four
words shared with the text in the three resource files, and the same check
was run against the specification's chapters, which stay out of this
repository. The specification remains the authority on what FIXP says.

The site fixtrading.org has terms of its own, which bar automated copying of
its content. Nothing here was taken from that site, and the upstream watch
reads only GitHub.

The schema's free-text slots, such as reason_text and description, hold
whatever their user writes into them. Fill them only with text you have the
right to use. The Apache License of this repository does not cover FIX's
text.

